# Findings

## High — Required process evidence remains unrecorded

The round-1 evidence gap is not resolved. `selected_command` is still captured but never emitted. The Pi launch still lacks a timestamped record equivalent to `opencode-info=... commands=... group=...`, and the pre/post-reload identity, command, and group values are still compared only through silent `test` commands. The newly added pre-exit records do not establish the required launch snapshot or expose both sides of reload continuity. Emit the selected VLC command, both hosts' launch snapshots (including shell PID, foreground identity/commands, PGID/group, and owned peer row), and the Pi before/after reload snapshots.

## Medium — The checkpoint is still not the first post-reload-readiness action

The successful readiness branch still prints `pi-reload-ready`, assigns `reload_ready`, and breaks; the script then tests that variable before calling `checkpoint post-pi-reload-first-action`. This still contradicts the explicit ordered-work and acceptance requirement. Call the protected checkpoint immediately after the readiness condition succeeds, before logging or subsequent validation.

## Medium — Unrelated Apnea records remain outside the preservation gate

Gates A and C still accept arbitrary `.apnea/**` mutations because they reject only non-Apnea paths, while `jj status` is informational. The plan therefore cannot enforce its acceptance criterion that unrelated Apnea records remain untouched. Add a before/after allowlist or checksum comparison that permits only dispatch-owned artifacts and legitimate orchestrator-owned mutable records.
